<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="CircuitRF.Ui.Views.Dialogs.AdoptExistingHistoryDialog"
        Title="This workspace already keeps a history"
        Width="560"
        SizeToContent="Height"
        MinHeight="260"
        CanResize="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        ShowInTaskbar="False">

    <!--
      §12 Q4 Refinement 3 (RC-6 R-rc6-7a). THE WORKSPACE-ROOT CASE IS A QUESTION, NOT AN OFFER.

      rev 3 offered adoption as a one-click action and never said what the user was choosing between.
      The user is asked, told what keeping their own configuration COSTS, and encouraged to adopt
      circuitRF's. Three answers, not two — the third is the hold state, which stays available.

      TWO THINGS THIS DIALOG IS BUILT AROUND:

        1. The consequences of "keep my settings" are stated AT THE POINT OF CHOOSING, and they are
           RECOVERABILITY consequences rather than tidiness ones — a fortnight instead of the promised
           weeks, and an escape hatch gone at thirty days. Listing configuration keys at a reader who
           did not come for them is not stating a consequence.

        2. The line that must be drawn or "keep my settings" is read as "and run my hooks": the answer
           governs REPOSITORY CONFIGURATION ONLY. Bypassing a hook is not a setting anyone can keep,
           because it is not a property of the repository — it is the rule that an automatic recording
           must neither fire somebody's tooling nor be blocked by it. That sentence is at the foot,
           where it applies to all three answers.

      The recommended answer is the default button AND says so in its own label. Nothing here is
      destructive, so there is no reason to make the safe answer the awkward one.
    -->

    <Grid RowDefinitions="*,Auto" Margin="20,16,20,16">

        <StackPanel Grid.Row="0" Spacing="10">
            <TextBlock x:Name="HeadlineLabel"
                       FontSize="13" FontWeight="SemiBold" TextWrapping="Wrap"/>

            <TextBlock FontSize="12" TextWrapping="Wrap" Opacity="0.85"
                       Text="circuitRF keeps restore points so you can go back to how a workspace was earlier. It can look after this one's history for you, or leave your own settings exactly as they are."/>

            <TextBlock x:Name="CostHeadingLabel"
                       FontSize="12" FontWeight="SemiBold" TextWrapping="Wrap" Margin="0,6,0,0"
                       Text="If you keep your own settings:"/>

            <ItemsControl x:Name="CostList" Margin="8,0,0,0">
                <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                    <DataTemplate>
                        <TextBlock Text="{Binding}" FontSize="12" TextWrapping="Wrap"
                                   Opacity="0.85" Margin="0,0,0,4"/>
                    </DataTemplate>
                </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
            </ItemsControl>

            <TextBlock x:Name="SurvivesLabel"
                       FontSize="12" TextWrapping="Wrap" Opacity="0.7" Margin="0,4,0,0"/>

            <TextBlock x:Name="SettingsOnlyLabel"
                       FontSize="11" TextWrapping="Wrap" Opacity="0.65"/>
        </StackPanel>

        <StackPanel Grid.Row="1" Orientation="Horizontal" HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                    Spacing="8" Margin="0,16,0,0">
            <Button x:Name="DeclineButton" FontSize="12" Padding="10,4"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    IsCancel="True"
                    Content="Don't keep a history here"
                    Click="OnDeclineClick"/>
            <Button x:Name="KeepButton" FontSize="12" Padding="10,4"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    Content="Keep my settings"
                    Click="OnKeepClick"/>
            <Button x:Name="AdoptButton" FontSize="12" Padding="10,4"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    IsDefault="True"
                    Content="Use circuitRF's settings (recommended)"
                    Click="OnAdoptClick"/>
        </StackPanel>
    </Grid>
</Window>
